# Working notes and tooling that live in this folder but are not part of the
# site. Without this file a `git add -A` swept an archive into a commit once,
# and Vercel then served it publicly.
elpys-project-context.md
elpys-opportunity-scout.zip
*.zip

# Patch files handed over for review; the changes land as commits, the
# patch itself is not part of the site.
*.patch

# Design source for the loading states. The CSS from it lives in styles.css
# and the markup builders in loading.js, so nothing here is needed to run the
# site. Left untracked because everything in this folder is served publicly by
# Vercel — committing it would put the design-tool export and its 69KB
# support.js on the live site as fetchable URLs.
loading animations/

# Secrets — none of these should ever be committed. Real values live in the
# Vercel project settings (SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, ADMIN_PASSWORD,
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY, CRON_SECRET, GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
.vercel/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Everything that is not the website. This folder is served from the repository
# root, so anything committed here becomes a public URL — which is how a skill
# archive ended up on the live site once (fixed in 568bb20). Keeping the whole
# working tree of prompts, patches, design sources, notes and logs under one
# ignored folder closes that off by construction rather than by remembering.
#
# Before this existed, .playwright-mcp/, docs/, claude/ and the design sources
# were all untracked but NOT ignored — one `git add -A` away from being live.
_work/

# The old locations, kept so that anything a tool recreates at the original path
# still never reaches the site. The scheduled data-check tasks in particular may
# write claude/ again on their own.
.playwright-mcp/
claude/
docs/
